Z||000018||Monkeyman||11-28-2001||06:04 PM||||yo_sweet--Creed has some Christian overtures, but they aren't considered a Christian band.  Scott Stapp (lead singer) is a Christian, but he claims that he doesn't bring his religion into his music.  Of course, it's fairly obvious if you listen to the words that his music is very Christian like.  At least they sing about "good" stuff instead of death, violence, rape, etc, etc like most of the other main stream bands.  (BTW--Creed has a new CD coming out!  I can't wait.  I might even give up smoking for a few days so I can afford the CD.)<P>The only non-Christian lyrics I've heard from Creed is GD (ain't gonna say it--nobody else better say it, either) in......can't remember the song right now.  He says it 4 or 5 times.  That bothers me.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||PAUL88GT||11-28-2001||06:51 PM||||DC Talk's "In the Light" is one of my favorite songs.  I am long time rock-n-roll and metal listener.  Christian Rock has improved greatly over the last few year.  I primarily listen to a station out of Nashville that is re-boosted in my area.  My kids like it too.  It is one area where we connect well.  However, just like pop music, a few songs get played over and over.<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Heretic||11-28-2001||07:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baptistheart:<BR><B>P.O.D. is about as hard as you get.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I sure do hope you're talking about as hard as you get in Christian rock. 'Cause if not , you need to look into some Slipknot and Testament...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hereticsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||TRiAD||11-28-2001||07:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Heretic:<BR><B> I sure do hope you're talking about as hard as you get in Christian rock. 'Cause if not , you need to look into some Slipknot and Testament...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hehe, try Argyle Park or Circle of Dust...Maybe Chagall Guavara (if you can find it), Oh, how could I forget Leaderdogs of the Blind...I've played with Lyndon Perry several times...you could search for KDOT, I was on their first EP...<P>But Argyle and Circle are as hard as anything you'll find, even in the secular market...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Brandon86SE||11-28-2001||11:35 PM||||OOH BOY!  You had to go and get me started!  I've been listening to Christian Punk Rock and Christian Heavy stuff for years, and I'd say a good number of the best punk bands out there are!  Ok, to start, lets go with the bands I have CD's for:  MxPx, Slick Shoes, Dogwood, Ghoti Hook, The Undecided, Value Pac, POD, Bleach, Stavesacre, Squad 5-O, Craig's Brother.  Those are all heavy/punk bands.  I also have CD's for Five Iron Frenzy, Supertones, The W's, for example are all ska/swing bands.  If you're interested in Christian heavy/punk check out  <A HREF="http://www.toothandnail.com" TARGET=_blank>www.toothandnail.com</A> , they are the premiere record company for that genre in Christian music.  All those examples are just the punk/heavy stuff.  Also GREAT Christian rock bands include Newsboys, DC Talk, Collective Soul (yes they are).......  I could go on.  If anyone has questions on this topic feel free to ask, chances are I'll know!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000023||soup||11-29-2001||12:39 AM||||well even though Creed does not call themselvs a "Christian" rock band they are. There first EP was produced on a christian label, and their songs off (I think the first CD was My OWn Prison, can't remember right now) their first cd had extreme christian overtones, but you are right, Scott came out after their first CD and said officially they are not a christian rock band.<P>I am not sure what band that was you heard but if you like christian rock definately check out P.O.D.||||reg||1
